# Privacy Policy for Remote Shutter

**Last updated: March 2, 2026**

## Overview

Remote Shutter ("the App") is developed by Security Union. This privacy policy explains how we handle information when you use our app.

## Data Collection

Remote Shutter operates primarily as a peer-to-peer camera remote control. The App:

- **Does not collect personal data** — No accounts, logins, or personal information are required.
- **Does not transmit data to external servers** — Photos and video are transferred directly between your paired devices over a local peer-to-peer connection (MultipeerConnectivity).
- **Does not track you** — We do not use analytics or tracking SDKs beyond what is required for ads.

## Camera and Microphone Access

The App requires camera and microphone access to function as a remote camera. This data is:
- Used only for the intended camera/video functionality
- Transferred only between your locally paired devices
- Never uploaded to any server

## Advertising

The App uses Google AdMob to display ads. Google may collect certain device information for ad personalization. You can review Google's privacy policy at https://policies.google.com/privacy. You may opt out of personalized ads through your device settings.

## In-App Purchases

In-app purchases are processed by Apple and subject to Apple's privacy policy.

## Contact

If you have questions about this privacy policy, please open an issue at https://github.com/security-union/remote-shutter/issues.

## Changes

We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Updates will be posted in this repository.
